<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Foulpointe</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mahavelona</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Foulpointe, in Malagasy Mahavelona, is a coastal town on the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toamasina">Toamasina</a>. In the 18th century it was a leading port of the Betsimisaraka coast, where French traders bought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and slaves for the Mascarene Islands. After the Merina conquest of the east coast, a round stone fort was built there in the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/foulpointe.jpg" alt="Foulpointe" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Souvaroff · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foulpointe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
